   "evidence": "In Levels.lean, `hadm` is a local `have` whose fields (`eq_of_isMIntegralCurve`, `exists_isOpen_isMaxOn`, \u2026) are built inline. The PR description says 'this PR supplies the admissibility construction that the monotonicity proof of Proposition 6.3 consumes'. The roadmap target is DGFloer/README.md:1102, Proposition 6.3.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Symplectic/Capacity/Levels.lean",
   "fix": "Extract a public theorem, e.g. `IsNondegenerate.isContractibleHZAdmissible_comp`, for any smooth antitone `\u03bc \u2265 0` with `\u03bc = 0` on `[b, \u221e)`, `\u03bc` constant on `(-\u221e, a]`, `|\u03bc'| \u2264 \u03c4` and `\u03bc' = 0` off `(a, b)`, under the same no-short-orbit hypothesis `horb`, concluding `\u03c3.IsContractibleHZAdmissible W (\u03bc \u2218 F)`. Then derive the capacity bound from it.",
   "issue": "The admissibility of `\u03bc \u2218 F` (`have hadm : \u03c3.IsContractibleHZAdmissible W (\u03bc \u2218 F)`) is buried inside the proof of `ofReal_mul_sub_le_contractibleHZCapacity`. The PR names this construction as what the remaining Prop 6.3 monotonicity proof will use, yet no declaration exposes it, and the private helper `eq_of_isMIntegralCurve_comp` can only be reached through this one proof.",
   "line": 165
  }
